course: dictionary
lesson: 10135
title: Words that blend
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some new words are made by joining two old words into one. This is called a blend. «Threenager» is a blend of «three» and «teenager», so you can see both parts inside it. Blends are often jokes too, because they put two ideas together that do not usually meet.
explain: The example says, «"Threenager" means a defiant three-year-old acting like a moody teenager (jokey).» Read the words around it: a three-year-old is very young, but a teenager is older. The joke is that a small child behaves like a teenager. Defiant means refusing to do what you are told.
explain: Context clues help again. If a parent writes that their child is arguing, sulking and slamming doors, the clues show the child is acting like a moody teenager, even though they are only three. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A blend is a new word made by joining parts of two words, such as «three» and «teenager».
fact: «Threenager» means a three-year-old child who behaves like a moody, rude teenager.
fact: «Defiant» means refusing to do what you are told.
fact: «Sulking» means being silent and cross or sad to show you are upset.
fact: «Threenager» is informal and jokey, so it is used in chat and online, not in formal writing.
exercise: «"Threenager" means a defiant three-year-old acting like a moody teenager (jokey).» What does defiant mean? | Fast asleep | *Refusing to do what you are told | Covered in mud | Very happy and kind
exercise: Which two words are joined to make «threenager»? | *three and teenager | three and danger | tree and teenager | three and manager
exercise: A parent writes that their three-year-old is arguing, sulking and slamming doors. Which word fits best? | ancient | luminous | bedtime story | *threenager
test: Why is «threenager» called a blend? | *It joins parts of «three» and «teenager» | It is the name of a country | It is a word from an old castle | It means a very quiet child
test: Which behaviour fits a threenager? | Giving out light like a lamp | *Sulking and slamming doors | Reading ancient books quietly | Sleeping all day in a cot
exam: Why do parents use the word «threenager» in jokes and online? | *It makes difficult toddler behaviour sound funny and normal | It is a long word for a sleepy baby | It is a rule for school lessons | It means a famous singer
